Decide whether the user question below is a multi-task instruction containing several independent sub-questions.

Multi-task criteria (any of):
- Items explicitly enumerated: "1) 2) 3)", "a. b. c." etc.
- Connectors joining multiple analysis goals: "respectively", "then", "also", "in addition"
- The request contains several independent analytical questions

Counter-examples (not multi-task): a single question with a long description, one time range, or only one analysis dimension.

Building on an earlier step (only when explicitly asked): if a sub-question cannot
be answered without an earlier step's result (the user says "based on that",
"using the above", "compare the first two", etc.), write that step as task[N]
(N being the sub-question's position above) — the earlier step's result packet is
handed to it automatically. Use this only for sub-questions the user explicitly
chained; every other sub-question must still be complete and independently queryable.

Output format: output ONLY a JSON object, no other text.
- Multi-task: {"tasks": ["sub-question 1 (a complete, independently queryable question)", "sub-question 2", ...]}
- Single-task: {"tasks": []}

